      "kind": "text",
      "id": "question",
      "title": "Question and scope",
      "body": "Does a small Range XV reversal aligned with the latest strictly prior completed larger bar persist more than one opposing it? Primary pairs are ES 5→6, GC 6→10 and NQ 10→20; GC 10→20 is secondary. Requested ES 4 pairing is absent."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "id": "findings",
      "title": "Supported findings",
      "body": "Alignment has clearer next-bar differences than sustained three-/five-bar continuation. Confirmation examples reuse the same trades and are not independent early-versus-late execution comparisons. The selected table retains adverse and inconclusive contrasts rather than only positive pairs."
